/*!
\page page_strndmhitcollection StRnDHitCollection — Collection Documentation

\section rnd_overview Overview

\ref StRnDHitCollection is a generic hit collection for
<b>Research and Development (R&D)</b> detector prototyping in STAR.  It is not
tied to any specific production sub-detector; instead it provides a flexible,
polymorphic container for \ref StRnDHit objects.

\ref StRnDHit extends \ref StHit with layer/ladder/wafer indices, up to eight
user-defined \c double values, and a custom error matrix, making it suitable for
prototyping new detector geometries and reconstruction algorithms without
requiring a dedicated collection class.

\section rnd_ownership Object Ownership

<b>mHits</b> (\c StSPtrVecRnDHit) is <b>owned</b>.  Unlike most other STAR
collections, the destructor <b>explicitly iterates and deletes</b> each element
individually.  This is necessary because \ref StRnDHit provides its own
\c operator \c new / \c operator \c delete via \c StMemoryPool, and the
container is polymorphic.

The collection itself is owned by the \c StEvent framework.

\section rnd_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecRnDHit | mHits | Container of \ref StRnDHit pointers.  Each hit carries: 3-D position and error, hardware position, charge, track reference count, MC truth ID/quality, detector ID (\c StDetectorId), layer/ladder/wafer indices, and up to eight prototype-specific \c double values. |

\section rnd_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c hits() | Reference to the hit collection (mutable and const overloads). |
| \c addHit(StRnDHit*) | Appends a hit; returns \c true on success, \c false if null. |
| \c numberOfHits() const | Returns the number of hits in the collection. |

\section rnd_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StRnDHitCollection* rndColl = event->rndHitCollection();
if (!rndColl || rndColl->numberOfHits() == 0) return;

const StSPtrVecRnDHit& hits = rndColl->hits();
for (size_t i = 0; i < hits.size(); ++i) {
    StRnDHit* hit = hits[i];
    unsigned int layer  = hit->layer();
    unsigned int ladder = hit->ladder();
    unsigned int wafer  = hit->wafer();
    float        charge = hit->charge();
}
\endcode

\see StRnDHit, StHit
*/
